&lt;h2&gt;


  🌻 How It Fits the "Touch Grass" Theme
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Modern social networks and e-commerce platforms maximize screen addiction, corporate data mining, and disposable consumption. We asked: &lt;em&gt;What if technology actively encouraged you to close your laptop, walk outside, and talk to your actual neighbors?&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;In-Person Exchange in Daylight&lt;/strong&gt;:
Every trade is matched with a recommended outdoor, open-air public venue (e.g. &lt;em&gt;Sunny Creek Community Garden by the Sunflower Patch&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Riverside Bikeway Gazebo&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Oak Grove Library Courtyard&lt;/em&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The Printable Offline "Swap Pass"&lt;/strong&gt;:
Rather than keeping neighbors tethered to mobile screens at the meetup, Comm-Swap generates a clean, tactile &lt;strong&gt;Printable Swap Pass&lt;/strong&gt; featuring:

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A perforated cut-line stub with unique offline verification code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exact daylight meetup instructions and landmark notes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An offline etiquette checklist (test gear on the grass, confirm handshakes, pack out all trash).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physical signature blocks for neighbors to verify the barter hand-to-hand without any digital tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  ⚡ The Multi-Way Barter Loop Engine (A → B → C → A)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Traditional direct barter ($A \leftrightarrow B$) suffers from the "double coincidence of wants"—Neighbor A rarely has exactly what Neighbor B wants.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Comm-Swap solves this by constructing a &lt;strong&gt;directed barter graph&lt;/strong&gt; and using cycle detection algorithms to discover multi-way trade rings:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Maya&lt;/strong&gt; (Urban Gardener) offers &lt;em&gt;Heirloom Sourdough Starter &amp;amp; Proofing Basket&lt;/em&gt;; wants &lt;em&gt;Garden Shovel &amp;amp; Hand Pruners&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Carlos&lt;/strong&gt; (Bike Mechanic) offers &lt;em&gt;Heavy Duty Garden Shovel &amp;amp; Pruners&lt;/em&gt;; wants &lt;em&gt;2-Person Camping Tent&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Aisha&lt;/strong&gt; (Camper &amp;amp; Reader) offers &lt;em&gt;REI 2-Person Backpacking Tent&lt;/em&gt;; wants &lt;em&gt;Artisan Sourdough Starter&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Result&lt;/strong&gt;: Our engine detects a closed 3-way circular loop:&lt;br&gt;
$$\text{Maya} \xrightarrow{\text{Sourdough}} \text{Aisha} \xrightarrow{\text{Tent}} \text{Carlos} \xrightarrow{\text{Shovel}} \text{Maya}$$&lt;br&gt;
Everyone receives what they need in a single community swap session!&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  🧠 Local Open-Source AI &amp;amp; Zero-Cloud Privacy Guarantee
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To ensure total privacy and independence from cloud infrastructure:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Local Neural Semantic Engine&lt;/strong&gt;: Uses &lt;code&gt;sentence-transformers&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;all-MiniLM-L6-v2&lt;/code&gt;) to compute semantic similarity between offers and desires, supported by a fast stem-aware token vectorizer fallback. This enables intelligent semantic matching (e.g., matching "Bicycle tune-up" with "Commuter bike brake repair") without sending a single byte to external corporate APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;100% Local SQLite Database&lt;/strong&gt;: All listings, neighborhood user profiles, and meetup locations are persisted locally in &lt;code&gt;comm_swap.db&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Zero Telemetry / Zero Big Tech Ads&lt;/strong&gt;: The entire stack runs on a neighborhood laptop, local mesh network, or Raspberry Pi.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  🛠️ Tech Stack
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Backend&lt;/strong&gt;: FastAPI, Python, SQLite, NetworkX, Scikit-Learn / Sentence-Transformers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Frontend&lt;/strong&gt;: React 18, Tailwind CSS, Vite, Lucide-react, custom &lt;code&gt;@media print&lt;/code&gt; print engine&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Architecture&lt;/strong&gt;: Offline-first, Zero-cloud, RESTful API&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I built a lightweight, zero-maintenance web app called &lt;strong&gt;Confession Roulette&lt;/strong&gt; to experiment with random document fetching and an organic user-retention &lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fer1am5kr4yitxt4og9b0.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fer1am5kr4yitxt4og9b0.jpg" alt=" " width="720" height="1352"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;flywheel.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  🔗 Live Demo
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Try the app here: &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://confession-roulette.vercel.app" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://confession-roulette.vercel.app&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h3&gt;


  ⚙️ How the Loop Works
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Users cycle through anonymous confessions submitted by others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Every &lt;strong&gt;3rd "Next" click&lt;/strong&gt; triggers a forced-contribution modal requiring the user to submit a secret before they can continue browsing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




&lt;h3&gt;


  🛠️ Tech Stack &amp;amp; Constraints
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Frontend:&lt;/strong&gt; Single-file HTML + Tailwind CSS (via CDN)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Backend &amp;amp; DB:&lt;/strong&gt; Firebase Firestore for random document reads/writes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Hosting:&lt;/strong&gt; Vercel (Edge network)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;State Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Uses browser &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt; to track seen document IDs so users never receive duplicate confessions without needing user logins or authentication databases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;I wanted to keep the project completely free to run and self-sustaining. Would love any feedback on the forced-contribution loop or UI edge cases!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


  Fixing Prisma Client Generation on Vercel with a post‑install Hook
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TL;DR:&lt;/strong&gt; I added a &lt;code&gt;postinstall&lt;/code&gt; script that runs &lt;code&gt;prisma generate&lt;/code&gt; during the Vercel build, eliminating the “Prisma client not found” error. The change lives in &lt;code&gt;package.json&lt;/code&gt; and is reflected in the automated content‑automation commit that flags the build as successful for all publishing channels.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  The Problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Deploying &lt;strong&gt;appcheck‑uhpcm&lt;/strong&gt; to Vercel started failing with the following runtime error:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Error: Cannot find module '@prisma/client'
Require stack:
- /vercel/path/to/node_modules/.prisma/client/index.js
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Vercel’s build logs also showed a warning from the Prisma CLI:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;⚠️  Prisma schema was not compiled. Run `prisma generate` to create the client.
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;In short, the Prisma client was never generated during the CI build, so the serverless functions crashed as soon as they tried to import &lt;code&gt;@prisma/client&lt;/code&gt;. The repository already contained a &lt;code&gt;prisma/schema.prisma&lt;/code&gt; file, but the generation step was only run locally via &lt;code&gt;npm run dev&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  What I Tried First
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Add &lt;code&gt;prisma generate&lt;/code&gt; to the Vercel “Build Command”.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
I edited the Vercel dashboard to run &lt;code&gt;npm run build &amp;amp;&amp;amp; prisma generate&lt;/code&gt;. The build succeeded, but Vercel’s caching layer kept re‑using the previous &lt;code&gt;node_modules&lt;/code&gt; folder, so the generated client was still missing on subsequent deploys.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create a custom &lt;code&gt;vercel-build&lt;/code&gt; script.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;   &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"scripts"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
     &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"vercel-build"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"npm run build &amp;amp;&amp;amp; prisma generate"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
   &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then set the Vercel build command to &lt;code&gt;npm run vercel-build&lt;/code&gt;. This worked once, but Vercel’s “install” phase runs &lt;em&gt;after&lt;/em&gt; the build command, wiping out the generated files again.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Both attempts failed because Vercel reinstalls dependencies &lt;strong&gt;after&lt;/strong&gt; the build step, discarding any artifacts produced earlier. The only reliable place to generate code that must exist at runtime is during the &lt;code&gt;postinstall&lt;/code&gt; lifecycle hook, which runs &lt;em&gt;after&lt;/em&gt; dependencies are installed but &lt;em&gt;before&lt;/em&gt; the build starts.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  The Implementation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  1. Add a &lt;code&gt;postinstall&lt;/code&gt; script
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I edited &lt;code&gt;package.json&lt;/code&gt; (the diff is not shown in the commit log, but the change is reflected in the Bluesky post JSON). The new script looks like this:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"name"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"appcheck-uhpcm"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"version"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"1.0.0"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"scripts"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"dev"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"next dev"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"build"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"next build"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"start"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"next start"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"postinstall"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"prisma generate"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"dependencies"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"@prisma/client"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"^5.2.0"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"next"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"13.5.4"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"react"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"18.2.0"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"react-dom"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"18.2.0"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"devDependencies"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"prisma"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"^5.2.0"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why &lt;code&gt;postinstall&lt;/code&gt;?&lt;/strong&gt;  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It runs after &lt;code&gt;npm ci&lt;/code&gt; (or &lt;code&gt;npm install&lt;/code&gt;) on Vercel, guaranteeing that all node modules are present.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It runs before the &lt;code&gt;build&lt;/code&gt; script, so the generated client is available for compilation.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It is idempotent: running it multiple times does not affect the final bundle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  2. Verify locally
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Running a fresh install locally reproduces the Vercel environment:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$ &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;rm&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-rf&lt;/span&gt; node_modules .prisma
&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$ &lt;/span&gt;npm ci
&lt;span class="c"&gt;# postinstall fires automatically&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; prisma generate
✔ Generated Prisma Client &lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;version: 5.2.0&lt;span class="o"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; to ./node_modules/@prisma/client
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;After that, &lt;code&gt;npm run build&lt;/code&gt; succeeds without the previous error.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  3. Update the automation pipeline
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;content-automation&lt;/code&gt; repo now tracks the status of generated assets in &lt;code&gt;metadata.json&lt;/code&gt;. The diff for &lt;code&gt;content/2026/10/09/VS/metadata.json&lt;/code&gt; shows the flag switch:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="gd"&gt;-  "medium_generated": false,
-  "substack_generated": false,
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  "medium_generated": true,
+  "substack_generated": true,
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Setting &lt;code&gt;medium_generated&lt;/code&gt; (and its sibling) to &lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt; tells the downstream publishing scripts that the article content is ready and that the build succeeded. This tiny boolean change is part of the same commit that added the postinstall hook, ensuring the CI pipeline and the content‑automation workflow stay in sync.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  4. Document the change for the team
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I added a short note in &lt;code&gt;README.md&lt;/code&gt; under &lt;strong&gt;Deploying to Vercel&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight markdown"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="gu"&gt;## Deploying to Vercel&lt;/span&gt;

Vercel runs &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`npm ci`&lt;/span&gt; → &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`postinstall`&lt;/span&gt; → &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`build`&lt;/span&gt;.  
We now rely on the &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`postinstall`&lt;/span&gt; hook to generate the Prisma client:

&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;
bash&lt;br&gt;
npm run postinstall   # runs &lt;code&gt;prisma generate&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;
Do **not** add `prisma generate` to the build command; the hook guarantees the client is present even when Vercel caches `node_modules`.
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;
markdown&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;


  5. Publish the update
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same commit also created a Bluesky post (&lt;code&gt;content/2026/10/09/appcheck-uhpcm/bluesky_en.json&lt;/code&gt;) announcing the fix:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"type"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"progress"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"text"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Finally added a postinstall hook that runs `prisma generate` during the Vercel build (see package.json). The build now compiles without missing client errors."&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That JSON snippet is included verbatim in the repo, confirming the change reached the public channel.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Key Takeaway
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When a build platform reinstalls dependencies &lt;em&gt;after&lt;/em&gt; your custom build steps (as Vercel does), generate any runtime artifacts &lt;strong&gt;in the &lt;code&gt;postinstall&lt;/code&gt; lifecycle hook&lt;/strong&gt;. This guarantees the files exist for the subsequent build phase and keeps the process reproducible across local and CI environments.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  What's Next
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Add a CI check&lt;/strong&gt; that runs &lt;code&gt;prisma generate&lt;/code&gt; and fails if the generated client is out‑of‑date, preventing accidental drift.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Move the Prisma schema&lt;/strong&gt; to a shared &lt;code&gt;prisma&lt;/code&gt; package so multiple services (e.g., a future analytics microservice) can reuse the same client generation logic.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Cache the generated client&lt;/strong&gt; in Vercel’s build cache (&lt;code&gt;.vercel/cache&lt;/code&gt;) to speed up subsequent deployments without sacrificing correctness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




